1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:06,100
When an emergency happens, you get one phone and one voice.

2
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:10,200
But you need help from many people at once.

3
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:21,800
Panic makes every extra call harder.

4
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:27,700
Ek Awaaz turns that one voice into calm, coordinated action.

5
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:41,000
Speak in Hindi, Marathi, English, or a natural mix.

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:47,200
We listen, understand, and coordinate trusted test contacts.

7
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:56,000
As the caller speaks, their words appear live.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Location, injuries, people, and hazards are highlighted.

9
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The incident card fills itself in.

10
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,500
When the address is corrected, the old location is replaced.

11
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:22,000
Nothing moves forward until type and location are confirmed.

12
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:42,000
After confirmation, a second agent works in parallel.

13
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,000
It prepares tailored calls and sends a location link.

14
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Every step stays visible on the timeline.

15
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:01,200
No clear address? A landmark keeps the conversation moving.

16
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:06,700
Silent mode supports private yes-or-no and keypad answers.

17
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Every action becomes a timestamped incident report.

18
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:22,100
This build stays in demo mode: test numbers only.

19
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:29,900
Ek Awaaz. One voice, many calls. Built with Bolna for Symphony.
